Details
More and more clients now run in Cloud containers (PODs).

Although docker-entrypoint can be updated to start up TAFJ Session Monitor in phantom inside PODs, there are two issues :

1. Each POD has to host TAFJ Session Monitor which will use additional POD resource

2. Load Balancer random connect to some POD. It’s difficult to monitor all PODs in one central place

 

We can configure tafj.properties in pre-image kits to let each POD to send session detail to external VM:

# Enable the TAFJMonitorSession

temn.tafj.runtime.session.monitor.enable=true

# Host name or IP of where is the TAFJMonitorSession

temn.tafj.runtime.session.monitor.host=10.29.9.22

# TCP port of the TAFJMonitorSession

temn.tafj.runtime.session.monitor.port=8377

 

10.29.9.22 is IP of any VM where TAFJ Session Monitor will be started.

All PODs will connect to the above configured IP and PORT to send TAFJ session detail.

 

Access below URL to monitor all PODs sessions.

http://10.29.9.22:8370/SessionMonitor

Host shows POD name – t24-app… and autoscale-…
